      <p><strong>Important:</strong> You do not need to complete every level in order. The purpose is to gradually practice skills that feel challenging without forcing yourself into situations that feel unsafe.</p>

      <h2>3. Overcoming the Fear of Talking to Strangers</h2>
      <p>The biggest reason people hesitate to speak to strangers is fear — fear of awkwardness, rejection, or judgment. But that fear is mostly imaginary. Once you start talking, it almost always goes better than you expect.</p>

      <h3>3.1 Rejection Doesn’t Define You</h3>
      <p>When a stranger doesn’t respond well, it’s not a reflection of you — it’s just human variety. Confidence means not needing everyone’s approval. Every “failed” conversation teaches you resilience.</p>

